   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "Between the villi lie small pits, the crypts of Lieberkühn. Two cell types line them. Goblet cells secrete mucus. Enterocytes secrete water and electrolytes, about 1800 milliliters a day, at a pH of seven and a half to eight, helping neutralize acid from the stomach. Up on the villi, enterocytes do the reverse, reabsorbing water, electrolytes, and the end products of digestion."
  }
